Z||000000||Monkeyman||05-15-2000||10:30 AM||||Can I fit a set of 5 1/4" speakers in the dash?  I know I'd have to do some modifications.  What would I have to do?  How much different would 4" speakers sound?  (Going with either 5 1/4" separates or 4" separates.)  What about either 3 1/2" or 4" speakers mounting low in the false firewall for rear fill?  I know everyone has their own opinions.  I'll take them all!||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-15-2000||11:36 AM||||5 1/4s will fit.. you'll have to get a couple pieces of pressboard (stuff your door panels are made from) and make a plate to isolate the sound waves so they won't kill them selves. I have 4 4" MB Quarts up front on this same board. the car is too small to utilize rear fill properly. Just make sure what ever route you choose you use the correct crossover point on a decent amp so your not just tossing out sound... it makes a HUGE difference in quality and volume ability.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Flash Box||05-15-2000||01:12 PM||||I have a set of 6" Jensen I will part with if you would like to play around with something like that. I also have a Pioneer Din Cassette Deck. E-mail me if you or anyone else is interested, I can provide pictures.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-15-2000||02:38 PM||||OK.  Where do I put the "plate"?  Am I supposed to surround the bottom of the speakers or just use it to fill in what's left of the mounting hole?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-15-2000||02:44 PM||||Flash Box--I appreciate it, but I'm looking at getting a set of 5 1/4" separates.  I already have a great JVC cassette head unit.  I was kinda thinking about upgrading to a nice CD head unit, but the ones I like are out of my price range for the moment.<P>Eventually, I'll get a sub but I'm still trying to figure out where I'll mount it.  I don't want to lose any leg room and mounting it in the ECM cover seems to be way too expensive as well as maybe having problems with the ECM?  Who knows.  I have neither the money nor the desire for a competition system like Fierosound (and others) has.  I'll probably sink the amp into the false firewall behind one of the seats.  I had thought about trying to figure out a way to mount the CD changer in the ECM cover, but I figured:  1)  It probably won't work if it's sideways and 2)  The ECM might interfere with the player itself.  Any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Homicidal||05-15-2000||04:35 PM||||No, the ecm wouldn't be affected by the sub or the changer.<P>Put the changer in the a)passenger footwell or b) behind one of the seats.<P>They can work sideways, upside down, etc..  There are settings on my changer that allow it to work in any position.  ||||reg||1
